+	    hidden plain parts from the hit set);
+	  - the hull topsides, bow and foredeck are Solid: a rider who jumps out, or walks the deck, stands on the drawn
+	    deck. The drive footprint (WE_HalfLength / WE_HalfWidth: the shore stop, the exit spots, the dock checks)
+	    reaches the Solid parts' ends; anything drawn past them (a raked stem tip, a gun barrel, a sub's rudder) stays
+	    within ShoreMargin - 1 = 2 studs of WE_HalfLength (BuyPathStatic N12), so the stop (HalfLength + 3 ahead)
+	    fires before the drawn tip reaches the shore. Every Solid part is at or over Y 0.2, so the ride height stays
+	    the kit's; the kit's other collidable blocks stop colliding (step 4d);
+	  - a pointed, raked bow (two stacked V wedges; the landing craft keep a ramp bow and the hovercraft a round skirt),
+	    a red bottom under the boot line and flared topsides; the bigger ships a raised forecastle (sheer);
+	  - the helmsman sits INSIDE a wheelhouse / bridge / conning tower: its lower walls hide his hips and legs, his
