+	    0.5 taller avatar); passengers sit inside a deckhouse, a gun tub, a troop well, a sunken cockpit or a hull
+	    shelter, never on a roof; side-by-side riders sit 3.4 apart or staggered 1.2+ along the ship (fix1b); a
+	    submarine's helmsman and lookout sit in the sail with only their heads over the rim, its other crew low in the
+	    hull under open hatches (head and shoulders out) or fully inside a low missile deck;
+	  - every seat stands over a floor (feet over the deck) and inside the kit's collidable box (SeatKitInset), so the
+	    builder never clamps it;
+	  - a distinct silhouette and palette per ship; muzzle pieces on the main guns;
+	  - realistic but compressed size against the 5.2-stud avatar, inside the base dock limits: the dock basin is 50 x 70
